\fBgaps\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Configure the gaps between windows
.TP 4
\fBinput\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Configure input devices
.TP 4
\fBkeymap\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Manage keymaps
.TP 4
\fBlayout\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Operations over layouts
.TP 4
\fBoutput\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Operate on outputs
.TP 4
\fBscratchpad\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Manage scratchpads
.TP 4
\fBsession\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Session control
.TP 4
\fBspawn\fR [\fB\-\-mode\fR=\fIMODE\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fISTRING\fR \fIto\fR \fIKEYBIND\fR
Run \fISTRING\fR as a shell command, e\N'46'g\N'46', \fI/bin/sh \-c STRING\fR
.TP 4
\fBtag\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Operate on tag views
.TP 4
\fBwindow\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Operations over windows
.TP 4
\fBwm\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Window\-manager control
.SH "BORDER"
.P
Border configuration commands
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBcolor\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Set the window color for a given state
.TP 4
\fBwidth\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIWIDTH\fR
Configure the border width
.SH "BORDER COLOR"
.P
Set the window color for a given state
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBcaptured\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
Set the border color when the window state is captured
.TP 4
\fBfocused\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
Set the border color when the window state is focused
.TP 4
\fBswallowing\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
Set the border color when the window state is swallowing
.TP 4
\fBunfocused\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
Set the border color when the window state is unfocused
.TP 4
\fBurgent\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
Set the border color when the window state is urgent
.SH "BORDER COLOR CAPTURED"
.P
Set the border color when the window state is captured
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color captured\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOLOR\fR (required)
An RGBA or RGB color string\N'46' The following are equivalent: \fI7FB4CAFF\fR \fI7FB4CA\fR\N'46' May be prefixed with \fI#\fR or \fI0x\fR\N'46'
.SH "BORDER COLOR FOCUSED"
.P
Set the border color when the window state is focused
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color focused\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOLOR\fR (required)
An RGBA or RGB color string\N'46' The following are equivalent: \fI7FB4CAFF\fR \fI7FB4CA\fR\N'46' May be prefixed with \fI#\fR or \fI0x\fR\N'46'
.SH "BORDER COLOR SWALLOWING"
.P
Set the border color when the window state is swallowing
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color swallowing\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOLOR\fR (required)
An RGBA or RGB color string\N'46' The following are equivalent: \fI7FB4CAFF\fR \fI7FB4CA\fR\N'46' May be prefixed with \fI#\fR or \fI0x\fR\N'46'
.SH "BORDER COLOR UNFOCUSED"
.P
Set the border color when the window state is unfocused
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color unfocused\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOLOR\fR (required)
An RGBA or RGB color string\N'46' The following are equivalent: \fI7FB4CAFF\fR \fI7FB4CA\fR\N'46' May be prefixed with \fI#\fR or \fI0x\fR\N'46'
.SH "BORDER COLOR URGENT"
.P
Set the border color when the window state is urgent
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border color urgent\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOLOR\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOLOR\fR (required)
An RGBA or RGB color string\N'46' The following are equivalent: \fI7FB4CAFF\fR \fI7FB4CA\fR\N'46' May be prefixed with \fI#\fR or \fI0x\fR\N'46'
.SH "BORDER WIDTH"
.P
Configure the border width
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl border width\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIWIDTH\fR
.SH "CONFIG"
.P
Configuration operations
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl config\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBreset\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Restore the stock configuration
.SH "CONFIG RESET"
.P
Restore the stock configuration
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl config reset\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-all\fR
Reset rules, keybinds, modes, and window/output labels\N'46'
.SH "EXEC"
.P
Execute \fICOMMAND\fR as a shell command, e\N'46'g\N'46', \fI/bin/emacs \-\-eval "(scratch\-buffer\fR" )
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl exec\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fICOMMAND\fR…
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fICOMMAND\fR (required)
The \fICOMMAND\fR to execute\N'46'
.SH "GAPS"
.P
Configure the gaps between windows
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl gaps\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBinner\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
Set the size of the inner gaps
.TP 4
\fBouter\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
Set the size of the outer gaps
.TP 4
\fBoverview\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
Set the size of the gaps for overview mode\N'46' A new output does not keep the \fB\-\-all\fR value\N'46'
.SH "GAPS INNER"
.P
Set the size of the inner gaps
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl gaps inner\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fIINT_DELTA\fR (required)
May be either an absolute value (\fB6\fR), or an offset (\fB\-2\fR)
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-all\fR
Apply the change to every tag on every output\N'46' The value becomes the default for new outputs and tags\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR
Filter to outputs matching \fINAME\fR\N'46'
.SH "GAPS OUTER"
.P
Set the size of the outer gaps
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl gaps outer\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fIINT_DELTA\fR (required)
May be either an absolute value (\fB6\fR), or an offset (\fB\-2\fR)
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-all\fR
Apply the change to every tag on every output\N'46' The value becomes the default for new outputs and tags\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR
Filter to outputs matching \fINAME\fR\N'46'
.SH "GAPS OVERVIEW"
.P
Set the size of the gaps for overview mode\N'46' A new output does not keep the \fB\-\-all\fR value\N'46'
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl gaps overview\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINT_DELTA\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fIINT_DELTA\fR (required)
May be either an absolute value (\fB6\fR), or an offset (\fB\-2\fR)
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-all\fR
Apply the change to every tag on every output\N'46' The value becomes the default for new outputs and tags\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR
Filter to outputs matching \fINAME\fR\N'46'
.SH "INPUT"
.P
Configure input devices
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBcursor\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Configure the cursor appearance
.TP 4
\fBkeyboard\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Configure keyboard input
.TP 4
\fBlist\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
List input devices matching the search pattern\N'46'
.TP 4
\fBpointer\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Pointer operations and settings
.TP 4
\fBrules\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Manage input rules
.SH "INPUT CURSOR"
.P
Configure the cursor appearance
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input cursor\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBtheme\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fINAME\fR \fISIZE\fR
Set the XCursor theme to NAME and SIZE
.SH "INPUT CURSOR THEME"
.P
Set the XCursor theme to NAME and SIZE
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input cursor theme\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fINAME\fR \fISIZE\fR
.SH "INPUT KEYBOARD"
.P
Configure keyboard input
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input keyboard\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBlayout\-file\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIPATH\fR
Set keyboard keymap from XKB keymap file at PATH
.TP 4
\fBrepeat\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIRATE\fR \fIDELAY\fR
Set the keyboard repeat RATE (keys/sec) and DELAY (ms)
.SH "INPUT KEYBOARD LAYOUT-FILE"
.P
Set keyboard keymap from XKB keymap file at PATH
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input keyboard layout\-file\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIPATH\fR
.SH "INPUT KEYBOARD REPEAT"
.P
Set the keyboard repeat RATE (keys/sec) and DELAY (ms)
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input keyboard repeat\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIRATE\fR \fIDELAY\fR
.SH "INPUT LIST"
.P
List input devices matching the search pattern\N'46'
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input list\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-expand\fR
Do not truncate cell values\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-fields\fR=\fIFIELDS\fR
Comma\-separated list of columns to show\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-case\fR
Match \fIPATTERN\fR case\-insensitively\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the raw JSON reply\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-name\fR=\fIREGEX\fR
Match \fIREGEX\fR, a PCRE regex, against the device name\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-role\fR=\fIROLE\fR
Filter to devices with this role\N'46' The value is one of \fBkeyboard\fR, \fBmouse\fR, \fBtouchpad\fR, \fBtouch\fR or \fBtablet\fR
.SH "INPUT POINTER"
.P
Pointer operations and settings
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBfollow\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
How pointer motion changes focus
.TP 4
\fBwarp\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
Whether keyboard focus changes warp the pointer
.SH "INPUT POINTER FOLLOW"
.P
How pointer motion changes focus
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer follow\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBalways\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Set the focus follows pointer policy to always
.TP 4
\fBcycle\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Cycle the focus follows pointer policy
.TP 4
\fBnever\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Set the focus follows pointer policy to never
.TP 4
\fBnot\-scrolling\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Set the focus follows pointer policy to not\-scrolling
.SH "INPUT POINTER FOLLOW ALWAYS"
.P
Set the focus follows pointer policy to always
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer follow always\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER FOLLOW CYCLE"
.P
Cycle the focus follows pointer policy
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer follow cycle\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER FOLLOW NEVER"
.P
Set the focus follows pointer policy to never
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer follow never\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER FOLLOW NOT-SCROLLING"
.P
Set the focus follows pointer policy to not\-scrolling
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer follow not\-scrolling\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER WARP"
.P
Whether keyboard focus changes warp the pointer
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer warp\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBoff\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Turn warp\-on\-focus off
.TP 4
\fBon\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Turn warp\-on\-focus on
.TP 4
\fBtoggle\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Toggle warp\-on\-focus
.SH "INPUT POINTER WARP OFF"
.P
Turn warp\-on\-focus off
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer warp off\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER WARP ON"
.P
Turn warp\-on\-focus on
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer warp on\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT POINTER WARP TOGGLE"
.P
Toggle warp\-on\-focus
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input pointer warp toggle\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SH "INPUT RULES"
.P
Manage input rules
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input rules\fR \fICOMMAND\fR …
.SS COMMANDS
.TP 4
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-expand\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR=\fIFIELDS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]…
List the input rules
.TP 4
\fBmouse\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Add or update a mouse rule
.TP 4
\fBremove\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINDEX\fR
Remove an input rule
.TP 4
\fBtouchpad\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
Add or update a touchpad rule
.SH "INPUT RULES LIST"
.P
List the input rules
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input rules list\fR [\fB\-\-expand\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR=\fIFIELDS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-expand\fR
Do not truncate cell values\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-fields\fR=\fIFIELDS\fR
Comma\-separated list of columns to show\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the raw JSON reply\N'46'
.SH "INPUT RULES MOUSE"
.P
Add or update a mouse rule
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input rules mouse\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-accel\-profile\fR=\fIPROFILE\fR
Set the pointer acceleration profile\N'46' The value is one of \fBnone\fR, \fBflat\fR, \fBadaptive\fR or \fBcustom\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-accel\-speed\fR=\fISPEED\fR
Set the pointer acceleration speed\N'46' The range is \-1\N'46'0 to 1\N'46'0\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-case\fR
Match \fIPATTERN\fR case\-insensitively\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-left\-handed\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the left\-handed button layout\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-middle\-emulation\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable middle\-button emulation\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-name\fR=\fIREGEX\fR
Match \fIREGEX\fR, a PCRE regex, against the device name\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-natural\-scroll\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the natural scroll direction\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-button\fR=\fIBUTTON\fR
Set the button that starts on\-button\-down scroll\N'46' The value is one of \fBBtn_0\fR, \fBBtn_1\fR, \fBBtn_2\fR, \fBBtn_3\fR, \fBBtn_4\fR, \fBBtn_5\fR, \fBBtn_6\fR, \fBBtn_7\fR, \fBBtn_8\fR, \fBBtn_9\fR, \fBBtn_left\fR, \fBBtn_right\fR, \fBBtn_middle\fR, \fBBtn_side\fR, \fBBtn_extra\fR, \fBBtn_forward\fR, \fBBtn_back\fR or \fBBtn_task\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-button\-lock\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the scroll button lock\N'46' With the lock, the scroll button toggles, and you do not hold it\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-factor\fR=\fIFACTOR\fR
Multiply the scroll distance by \fIFACTOR\fR\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-method\fR=\fIMETHOD\fR
Set the scroll method of the device\N'46' The value is one of \fBno\-scroll\fR, \fBtwo\-finger\fR, \fBedge\fR or \fBon\-button\-down\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-send\-events\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Set the send\-events mode of the device\N'46' The value is one of \fBenabled\fR, \fBdisabled\fR or \fBdisabled\-on\-external\-mouse\fR
.SH "INPUT RULES REMOVE"
.P
Remove an input rule
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input rules remove\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIINDEX\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fIINDEX\fR (required)
The rule index from the \fBlist\fR output\N'46'
.SH "INPUT RULES TOUCHPAD"
.P
Add or update a touchpad rule
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl input rules touchpad\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-accel\-profile\fR=\fIPROFILE\fR
Set the pointer acceleration profile\N'46' The value is one of \fBnone\fR, \fBflat\fR, \fBadaptive\fR or \fBcustom\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-accel\-speed\fR=\fISPEED\fR
Set the pointer acceleration speed\N'46' The range is \-1\N'46'0 to 1\N'46'0\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-click\-method\fR=\fIMETHOD\fR
Set the click method of the touchpad\N'46' The value is one of \fBnone\fR, \fBbutton\-areas\fR or \fBclickfinger\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-clickfinger\-button\-map\fR=\fIBUTTON\fR
Set the button order for clicks with one, two, or three fingers\N'46' The value is either \fBleft\-right\-middle\fR or \fBleft\-middle\-right\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-\-disable\-while\-trackpointing\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the disable\-while\-trackpointing feature\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-disable\-while\-typing\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the disable\-while\-typing feature\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-drag\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable tap\-and\-drag\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-drag\-lock\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Set the drag lock mode for tap\-and\-drag\N'46' The value is one of \fBdisabled\fR, \fBenabled\-timeout\fR or \fBenabled\-sticky\fR
.TP 4
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-case\fR
Match \fIPATTERN\fR case\-insensitively\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-left\-handed\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the left\-handed button layout\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-middle\-emulation\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable middle\-button emulation\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-name\fR=\fIREGEX\fR
Match \fIREGEX\fR, a PCRE regex, against the device name\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-natural\-scroll\fR=\fIOPTION\fR
Enable or disable the natural scroll direction\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-factor\fR=\fIFACTOR\fR
Multiply the scroll distance by \fIFACTOR\fR\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-scroll\-method\fR=\fIMETHOD\fR
