.SH "TAG QUERY"
.P
Query the tag state of output
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl tag query\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]…
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-expand\fR
Do not truncate cell values\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-fields\fR=\fIFIELDS\fR
Comma\-separated list of columns to show\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the raw JSON reply\N'46'
.TP 4
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fINAME\fR
Filter to outputs matching \fINAME\fR\N'46'
.SH "TAG TOGGLE"
.P
Toggle the visibility of \fITAGS\fR
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl tag toggle\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fITAGS\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fITAGS\fR (required)
Tags are numbered 1 to 32\N'46' They may be named directly as indices: a single tag (\fB7\fR), a comma\-separated list (\fB1,3,8\fR), or a range (\fB1\-3,5\fR)\N'46' They may also be given as a bitmask in hexadecimal (\fB0xff\fR), binary (\fB0b101\fR), or octal (\fB0o17\fR), where each set bit selects one tag\N'46' Note that \fB7\fR means tag 7, while \fB0b111\fR means tags 1, 2, and 3\N'46'
.SH "TAG VIEW"
.P
View a set of \fITAGS\fR
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl tag view\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fITAGS\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fITAGS\fR (required)
Tags are numbered 1 to 32\N'46' They may be named directly as indices: a single tag (\fB7\fR), a comma\-separated list (\fB1,3,8\fR), or a range (\fB1\-3,5\fR)\N'46' They may also be given as a bitmask in hexadecimal (\fB0xff\fR), binary (\fB0b101\fR), or octal (\fB0o17\fR), where each set bit selects one tag\N'46' Note that \fB7\fR means tag 7, while \fB0b111\fR means tags 1, 2, and 3\N'46' The string literal \fIoccupied\fR is allowed and represents all currently occupied tags\N'46'
.SH "UNBIND"
.P
Unbind the given KEYBIND
.SS SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBoxctl unbind\fR [\fB\-\-mode\fR=\fIMODE\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fIKEYBIND\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fIKEYBIND\fR (required)
Modifiers, keysym, and/or button\N'46' Modifiers include Shift, Control, Mod1/Alt, Mod3, Mod4/Super/Logo, Mod5, or None\N'46' Keysyms mirror xkbcommon\-keysym\N'46'h without the \N'39'K_\N'39' prefix, (e\N'46'g\N'46' Return instead of K_Return)\N'46' Buttons are prefixed with \N'39'Btn_\N'39' followed by [0\-9], left, right, middle, side, extra, forward, back, or task\N'46'
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-mode\fR=\fIMODE\fR
The keymap mode the binding belongs to (default \fBnormal\fR)\N'46'
