.P
\fBoxctl window tag set\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]… \fITAGS\fR
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP 4
\fITAGS\fR (required)
Tags are numbered 1 to 32\N'46' They may be named directly as indices: a single tag (\fB7\fR), a comma\-separated list (\fB1,3,8\fR), or a range (\fB1\-3,5\fR)\N'46' They may also be given as a bitmask in hexadecimal (\fB0xff\fR), binary (\fB0b101\fR), or octal (\fB0o17\fR), where each set bit selects one tag\N'46' Note that \fB7\fR means tag 7, while \fB0b111\fR means tags 1, 2, and 3\N'46' The string literal \fIoccupied\fR is allowed and represents all currently occupied tags\N'46'
.SS OPTIONS
.TP 4
\fB\-\-all\fR
Act on every match\N'46'
